/* ---- self assessment ---- */
'自我评价':'Personal Statement',
'从史料，到图像，再到物质——我把三种训练串成一条互相校正的链条。历史学让我习惯从一手材料与现场提问，美术史让我学会读图、断代与辨伪，雕塑训练则逼我把结论交还给双手：想法必须能成型、能入窑、能站得住。三段学历不是三个标签的叠加，而是同一个问题在不同介质里的反复验证。':'From historical sources, to images, to material — I have tied three trainings into a single chain of mutual correction. History taught me to question through primary sources and the site itself; art history taught me to read images, date them and tell the genuine from the false; sculpture forces me to return every conclusion to my hands: an idea must be formable, must survive the kiln, must be able to stand. Three degrees are not three labels stacked up, but one question tested again and again in different media.',
'我把研究做"重"，也把创作做"实"。研究上，我习惯真正进入现场：量遗址、做口述、拍素材、建档案，再回到案头做图像学与文本分析；创作上，从泥料配比、釉料试验到烧成曲线，每一道工序都亲手完成。茂名的革命遗址普查、张田饼印、贵州村寨志、景德镇手工艺群体，田野给了我问题；龙泉工作室与昌马石窟临摹，给了我把它落成形体的能力。':'I do research the heavy way, and making the solid way. In research I go to the site: measuring ruins, recording oral accounts, shooting material, building archives, then returning to the desk for iconographic and textual analysis. In the studio, from clay body and glaze tests to the firing curve, every step is done by hand. The revolutionary-site survey in Maoming, the Zhangtian cake moulds, the Guizhou village gazetteer, the Jingdezhen handicraft community — the field gave me the questions; the Longquan studio and the Changma cave copies gave me the ability to turn them into form.',
'工具箱是一格格填满的。日语 N1 让我能直接处理日文文献与近代史料，英语支撑国际会议报告，拉丁语、苏美尔语与阿卡德语的训练则把更古老的材料纳入视野；AI 辅助质性研究、遥感考古与三维建模，是我为田野方法预留的更新接口。四十余项研修与认证，于我并非收藏，而是让每一个问题都能找到趁手的工具。':'The toolbox was filled one compartment at a time. JLPT N1 lets me work directly with Japanese sources and modern historical documents; English carries my international conference presentations; training in Latin, Sumerian and Akkadian brings far older material into view. AI-assisted qualitative research, remote-sensing archaeology and 3D modelling are the update ports I keep open for fieldwork method. Forty-odd programmes and certificates are not a collection to me — they mean every question can find a tool that fits the hand.',
'耐得住琐碎，也守得住工期。我能独立跑完从选题、田野、写作到成品的全流程，也能在团队里承担框架设计、访谈与影像记录的具体分工；在村子里能挨家挨户地聊，在工坊里能连续几周守着一座窑。面对遗产与手工艺，我倾向于先记录、再理解、最后才创作的次序。':'I can live with drudgery and I can hold a schedule. I run the whole chain myself — choosing a topic, fieldwork, writing, finished work — and I can also take a specific role in a team: research design, interviewing, film and photo documentation. In a village I can talk door to door; in a workshop I can keep watch over a kiln for weeks. Faced with heritage and handicraft, I prefer this order: record first, understand second, create last.',
'接下来的方向，是在文化遗产研究与陶瓷创作的交汇处继续深入——用田野的方法做研究，用陶瓷的语言做表达，让两者彼此校正、彼此成全。':'The direction ahead is to go deeper where cultural-heritage research meets ceramic practice: doing research by the methods of the field, expressing it in the language of clay, and letting the two correct and complete each other.',
