/* ---- 学术主线版式（2026-10 改版新增） ---- */
'美术史研究者 ✦ 文化遗产田野工作者 ✦ 陶瓷雕塑创作者':'Art Historian ✦ Cultural-Heritage Fieldworker ✦ Ceramic Sculptor',
'以学术研究为主业。历史学起步，美术史研究进阶，近年聚焦物质文化与手工艺、墓葬建筑图像、文化遗产的田野与数字化保护；陶瓷雕塑创作与多语种能力，是这条研究主线的延伸与校验。常驻浙江龙泉，长期从事田野调查与遗产研究。':'Research comes first. Trained in history, specialised in art history, and now focused on material culture and handicraft, funerary architectural imagery, and the fieldwork and digital documentation of cultural heritage; ceramic sculpture and multilingual competence extend and test that line of research. Based in Longquan, Zhejiang, long engaged in fieldwork and heritage research.',
'篇论文 · 5 次会议宣讲':'Papers · 5 conference presentations',
'项学术 · 调研类获奖':'Academic & field-survey awards',
'嵇鸿轩，1999 年生，':'Hongxuan Ji, born 1999, ',
'以学术研究为主业':'is first and foremost a researcher',
'。 本科就读历史学，硕士修读美术史研究（澳门科技大学），此后于景德镇陶瓷大学攻读雕塑（第二学士学位）， 完成':'. He read History as an undergraduate, took an MA in Art History at Macau University of Science and Technology, and then studied Sculpture at Jingdezhen Ceramic University as a second bachelor, completing ',
'"历史—美术史—创作"':'"history — art history — making"',
'的跨学科路径。 研究线索集中在三条：澳门墓葬建筑图像与中西视觉交融、粤西与黔东的非遗田野与口述史、景德镇陶瓷手工艺群体的生产与身份。 已以独立作者发表期刊论文 2 篇，并在香港岭南大学、英国爱丁堡大学、越南胡志明国家人文社科大学等会议作口头报告 5 次。':'an interdisciplinary path. His research runs along three threads: funerary architectural imagery and Sino-Western visual hybridity in Macao; intangible heritage, fieldwork and oral history in western Guangdong and eastern Guizhou; and the production and identity of the Jingdezhen handicraft community. He has published two journal articles as sole author and given five oral papers at conferences including Lingnan University (Hong Kong), the University of Edinburgh, and Ho Chi Minh City University of Social Sciences and Humanities (Vietnam).',
'研究兴趣':'Research Interests',
'物质文化与手工艺研究':'Material Culture & Handicraft Studies',
'墓葬建筑与图像学':'Funerary Architecture & Iconography',
'文化遗产数字化保护':'Digital Safeguarding of Cultural Heritage',
'非遗田野与口述史':'Intangible Heritage Fieldwork & Oral History',
'区域国别与跨文化交流':'Area Studies & Cross-Cultural Exchange',
'在此之外：2023 年起在浙江龙泉青瓷产地创办个人工作室常驻创作，代表作有《骏骨凝香》《瓦猫》《春日来信》《秘色》《蓝色血液》等， 作品入选省级雕塑大展并被艺术馆收藏；日语 N1、英语与拉丁语、苏美尔语、阿卡德语的训练，则让日文史料、国际会议与更古老的材料直接进入我的研究。':'Beyond that: since 2023 he has kept his own studio in Longquan, Zhejiang — the historic home of celadon — with representative works including Fragrance of Steed Bones, Tile Cat, Letter from Spring, Mise (Secret Colour) and Blue Blood, shown in provincial sculpture exhibitions and collected by an art museum; JLPT N1, English, and training in Latin, Sumerian and Akkadian let Japanese historical sources, international conferences and far older material feed straight into his research.',
'创作与技艺于我是加分项而非主线——它们让研究有手感，也让结论能被双手验证。':'Making and craft skills are a bonus rather than the main line — they give research a feel for the material, and let its conclusions be tested by hand.',
