tr_shouzhou:{tag:'Programme · 2026.07',title:'China National Arts Fund 2026 — Shouzhou Kiln Innovative Craft Talent Training',
 meta:[['Funding','China National Arts Fund 2026 arts talent training programme'],['Host','School of Art and Design, Huainan Normal University'],['Role','Admitted participant'],['Registration','4 Jul 2026 · Huainan, Anhui']],
 body:`<p>Admitted after expert panel review as a participant in the China National Arts Fund 2026 arts talent training programme Innovative Craft Talent Training for the Shouzhou Kiln. <b style="color:var(--gold-bright);font-weight:400">About the China National Arts Fund</b>: a national funding system established by the state and administered by the Ministry of Culture and Tourism which, together with the National Social Science Fund's arts programme, forms the highest level of arts funding in China. Its talent-training strand is open to national application, and only after eligibility screening and several rounds of anonymous expert review is a project funded and its participants admitted; places are limited and competition is intense nationwide, making it a widely recognised high-value national training credential in professional art practice. The programme focuses on the transmission and renewal of Shouzhou kiln porcelain technique, directly relevant to his ceramic practice and conservation work; in preparation he studied monographs including Shouzhou Kiln compiled by the Huainan Museum (Cultural Relics Press).</p>`,
 cap:['Letter of admission · China National Arts Fund / Huainan Normal University'],
 tags:['China National Arts Fund','Shouzhou kiln','Craft transmission']},
