 body:`<p>Japanese is a core research and translation tool: he passed level N1 of the Japanese-Language Proficiency Test in 2019 and has continued to translate and compete in Japanese — the "People's China" Cup, the Han Suyin International Translation Contest, the Liaoning translation contest, the "Ocean Cup" international contest — and has translated wartime Japanese military correspondence. In 2026 he passed the national College Japanese Test Band 6 (CJT-6). English serves academic exchange (oral presentations at several international conferences) and brought Third Prize in the English–Chinese section of the national cultural-relics diplomacy translation contest. From 2026 he has studied Latin, Sumerian and Akkadian as further research tools.</p>`,
